<title>GERMANY: Adtranz wins Russian rail order.</title>
<headline>Adtranz wins Russian rail order.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>European railway group Adtranz said on Friday the Russia Federation had placed an order for 21 locomotives worth 48 million Ecus.</p>
<p>Adtranz, a 50-50 joint venture between Germany's Daimler-Benz AG and Swiss/Swedish engineering firm ABB AB/AG, said it would begin delivering the electric engines in 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;This contract marks an essential breakthrough since we are the first western rail concern to sign a cooperation contract in Russia,&quot; said Heinz Cronimund, the Adtranz chief responsible for Russia.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
